    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-23T21:19:04+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T21:19:04+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T10:49:04Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T10:49:04Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure that lies near the NT/WA border will combine with a trough and cold front further south to move over much of SA from Saturday, and over the far northeast on Sunday. A ridge of high pressure will then move into the west from late Sunday and persist over the rest of the state throughout next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-23T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers south of Yunta, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm from the late morning, possibly severe with damaging winds and large hail south of Yunta in the afternoon and evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then tending north to northwesterly in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Leigh Creek, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds in the far northeast. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h before dawn then tending south to southwesterly 35 to 50 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower north of Oodnadatta in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the afternoon and evening. Winds south to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Leigh Creek, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta. Winds south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
